      "finding": "without approval",
      "explanation": "Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.",
      "remediation": "Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.",
      "code_snippet": "\nAsk only what changes the result: audience, job, primary action, real content/proof, constraints, success, what must not change, and what would make a polished result feel wrong. Resolve material unknowns before implementation; do not re-ask settled facts, request CSS values, or make a precise request pass through a concept tournament.\n\n**Local extension:** resolve the new content, hierarchy, interaction and states in context. Do not reopen identity or change durable design rules without approval.\n\n**Whole surface in an established world:** explore materially different organizations of the real task and content, not different skins. Consider five to seven structures internally when the brief is genuinely open; present two or three viable, distinct first-viewport concepts at equal detail. Explain navigation, work/reading areas, density, what leads and where the primary action lives. A representative screenshot of the incumbent product is a stronger identity anchor than a prose paraphra",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Excessive Agency"
      ],
      "evidence": {},
      "match_fingerprint": "7868080a35a6878aa292c53196ddb331f19d628c33953fb70850fdaf54c4191c",
